        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-026-04682-2">
            <title><![CDATA[Gene alteration in human brain suggests genetic and epigenetic roots of major depression]]></title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-026-04682-2</link>
            <content:encoded>
                <![CDATA[<p>Nature Medicine, Published online: 03 September 2026; <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-026-04682-2">doi:10.1038/s41591-026-04682-2</a></p>A large, multimodal molecular characterization of the adult human hippocampus provides evidence for sustained neurogenesis and identifies a stalled neurogenic process in major depressive disorder (MDD). Cell- and circuit-specific genetic, epigenetic, stress, immune, metabolic and synaptic mechanisms are identified that underlie impaired hippocampal plasticity, providing a framework for disease subtyping and therapeutic development.]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title><![CDATA[Gene alteration in human brain suggests genetic and epigenetic roots of major depression]]></dc:title>
            
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41591-026-04682-2</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Medicine, Published online: 2026-09-03; | doi:10.1038/s41591-026-04682-2</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-09-03</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Medicine</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41591-026-04682-2</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-026-04682-2</prism:url>
        </item>
    
