        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41591-026-00045-z">
            <title><![CDATA[Induced proximity comes of age]]></title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/d41591-026-00045-z</link>
            <content:encoded>
                <![CDATA[<p>Nature Medicine, Published online: 03 September 2026; <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41591-026-00045-z">doi:10.1038/d41591-026-00045-z</a></p>The first approved PROTAC for breast cancer validated the idea that medicines can work by bringing proteins together rather than by simply blocking them. Now, a new generation of proximity-based therapies is pushing that principle further.]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title><![CDATA[Induced proximity comes of age]]></dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Natalie Healey</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/d41591-026-00045-z</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Medicine, Published online: 2026-09-03; | doi:10.1038/d41591-026-00045-z</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-09-03</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Medicine</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/d41591-026-00045-z</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/d41591-026-00045-z</prism:url>
